.TH OMARCHY-NOTES-RUST 1 "October 2026" "omarchy-notes-rust 1.0.2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
omarchy-notes-rust \- private local notes
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B omarchy-notes-rust
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Omarchy Notes is an application for private local notes.
Version 1.0.2 provides rich writing, organization and recovery.
Its library and preferences retain the preview locations. The installed
.B omarchy-notes-preview
compatibility launcher executes the application with unchanged arguments.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-new
Create a note in this library's main window.
.TP
.BI \-\-note " UUID"
Open a specific note.
.TP
.B \-\-quick-note
Open or activate Quick Note.
.TP
.BI \-\-data-dir " PATH"
Open a compatible library at PATH. Use a copy and verified backup for Qt libraries.
.TP
.BI \-\-capture " TEXT"
Save durable capture text. A dash reads standard input. Works without a display.
.TP
.BI \-\-request-id " UUID"
Retry the same capture with its original request identity and text.
.TP
.BI \-\-capture-status " UUID"
Check a capture receipt without changing the library.
.TP
.BI \-\-backup " NEW-DIRECTORY"
Create a verified lossless backup. Close the running library owner first.
.TP
.BI \-\-inspect-backup " DIRECTORY"
Verify a completed backup without changing it.
.TP
.BI \-\-restore " DIRECTORY"
Restore to a new destination supplied by \-\-data-dir. Existing libraries remain intact.
.TP
.B \-\-reference, \-\-light
Select graphite or warm paper appearance for this launch.
.TP
.B \-\-demo
Open disposable sample notes.
.TP
.B \-\-simulate-save-failure
Exercise recovery with a scratch library; not an ordinary writing option.
.TP
.B \-\-help, \-\-version
Show application help or version.
.SH KEYBOARD
Ctrl+N creates a note, Ctrl+S saves, Ctrl+K searches, Ctrl+, opens Settings,
and Ctrl+Backslash toggles focus mode. Ctrl+Shift+N opens Quick Note;
Ctrl+Shift+O moves Quick Note into the main window. Ctrl+Alt+N creates a folder.
In the folder tree, arrows navigate/expand/collapse, Home/End reach its edges,
and Enter opens the focused scope. Destructive actions require their focused
library controls; editor Delete remains text editing.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/omarchy-notes-gpui/
Default library, with ~/.local/share as the XDG fallback.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/omarchy-notes-gpui/preferences.json
Writing preferences, with ~/.config as the XDG fallback.
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/omarchy-notes-rust/
Private library-specific ownership and capture protocol.
.SH COMPATIBILITY
Tags and Smart Folder interfaces are deferred. Preserve their existing records
through backups. Quotation/schema-3 libraries require the current app. Returning to Qt uses
the verified pre-upgrade backup and excludes subsequent changes. Portable
Markdown/HTML exports can be lossy and do not replace lossless library backups.
.SH QUICK NOTE SETUP
The desktop launcher has a Quick Note action. Optional compositor shortcuts
should use a distinct key and the org.omarchy.Notes.Rust application identity;
the installer does not claim to modify compositor bindings automatically.
.SH SEE ALSO
https://github.com/last-refuge/omarchy-notes
